{"id": "EUVD-2026-102359", "enisaUuid": "62714f8a-c27c-338b-86e8-63e1de6712bf", "description": "Assimp through 6.0.5 contains a NULL pointer dereference vulnerability in the Ogre3D importer that allows attackers to crash applications via unvalidated bone indices in OgreStructs.cpp. Attackers can supply a crafted .mesh and .skeleton file referencing a missing bone, causing BoneById() to return null and crash the host process.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T18:57:24", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T19:45:45", "baseScore": 6.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/assimp-ogre-mesh-bone-submesh-null-deref", "https://github.com/assimp/assimp/blob/392a658f9c271be965271f45e7521a1b80ea4392/code/AssetLib/Ogre/OgreStructs.cpp#L621-L634", "https://github.com/assimp/assimp/blob/392a658f9c271be965271f45e7521a1b80ea4392/code/AssetLib/Ogre/OgreStructs.cpp#L914-L921", "https://github.com/assimp/assimp", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/assimp-through-6.0.5-null-pointer-dereference-via-ogre-importer-bone-assignment"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111128", "GHSA-qxj4-4wqq-r2q6"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "22c81a53-8bba-3d86-a7a9-5418c5c666d3", "product": {"name": "Assimp", "vendor": {"name": "Open Asset Import Library"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22646.0.5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "ca02442c-aa1a-3906-b557-46e149f69c32", "vendor": {"name": "assimp"}}], "isExploited": false}